1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,458
The missing voice arrived at the second step of the sports center, from an obese man who played badminton twice a week in the courtyard.

2
00:00:08,458 --> 00:00:13,797
“Your typical athlete is not the typical inhabitant,” he said.

3
00:00:13,797 --> 00:00:16,857
“I am not asking for splendor.

4
00:00:16,857 --> 00:00:29,830
I am asking for adequacy.” His genetic inheritance, he added, had given him a knee that hurt in the moist air and a dental bill he could not satisfy.

5
00:00:29,830 --> 00:00:36,094
The interpretation of the word health, he said, was doing the damage.

6
00:00:36,094 --> 00:00:52,867
“You interpret well-being as a personal project, and then you amuse yourselves with slogans.” A decorative bullet, a monumental poster, and a guitar in the corner of the auditorium were the whole of the previous campaign.

7
00:00:52,867 --> 00:00:59,406
The ugliness of it, he said, was the exclusion underneath.

8
00:00:59,406 --> 00:01:11,644
He asked them to donate one hour a week to a boxing class for people his size, and to notify the management that the fatality figures in the report were not an exaggeration.

9
00:01:11,644 --> 00:01:23,052
A westerner’s diet, a compensatory snack, and a cute cartoon about surfing had been used as evidence for a claim that no one could heal.

10
00:01:23,052 --> 00:01:33,765
The fuss about his weight, he said, was a distraction from a fatal assumption: that a person who cannot run has nothing to teach a club.

11
00:01:33,765 --> 00:01:42,549
The acting coach, the second site, and the large financial grant all arrived with the same prejudice built in.

12
00:01:42,549 --> 00:01:46,808
“Accustom yourselves to the slow,” he said.

13
00:01:46,808 --> 00:01:51,902
“Populate the class with people who are not like you.”

14
00:01:51,902 --> 00:02:03,981
The rest of the arc would follow his advice: a lunar calendar for the classes, a recovery step for every injury, and a north-lit room for the winter sessions.

15
00:02:03,981 --> 00:02:12,514
His life expectancy, he told them, was no shorter than theirs if the war against his own body stopped.

16
00:02:12,514 --> 00:02:18,404
He watched them from the south corner, and nobody in the room could answer him.

17
00:02:18,404 --> 00:02:23,118
“Do not let the big room disappear,” he advised.

18
00:02:23,118 --> 00:02:39,315
“A helpful class is not a comedy, and a slogan is nonsense unless it can compensate for a missing ramp.” He asked who would inhabit the courtyard in the winter, and whether a westerner could ever fit a segmental shift.

19
00:02:39,315 --> 00:02:47,974
The management, the financial office, and the large grant all heard him; them he trusted least of all.

20
00:02:47,974 --> 00:02:59,368
The church, the god of the timetable, the nation of the slow, and the north wind: or something like it, he said.
